diff --git a/docs/chat-bots.md b/docs/chat-bots.md
index 8ade8d2..cae74a7 100644
--- a/docs/chat-bots.md
+++ b/docs/chat-bots.md
@@ -2,6 +2,8 @@
 
 To create a bot, open **Account settings**, select **Set up chat bots**, then select **Add a chat bot**. The bots page shows the codes for the bots you manage. Administrators can manage all bots.
 
+Members can create up to five bots each by default. Administrators can change **Bots per member** in **Account settings** (set it to zero to stop members from creating bots). Lowering the limit keeps existing bots, but members can't create more until they're below the limit. Deleted bots don't count, and administrators aren't limited.
+
 By default, bots do not join any rooms. To give a bot access to a specific open or closed room, select it in that room’s membership settings. Turn on **Add to all open rooms** on the bot’s form to add it to existing open rooms and any rooms that become open later. Turning the switch off keeps the bot’s current memberships.
 
 Post text to a room the bot belongs to:
